WEBVTT

00:00.630 --> 00:02.740
At the dawn of the Seika era,

00:02.740 --> 00:05.980
in order to regulate unwanted messages that presented a bad influence to society,

00:05.980 --> 00:08.430
the Media Cleansing Act was passed.

00:09.310 --> 00:12.690
The libraries armed themselves in order to protect freedom of expression

00:12.690 --> 00:15.590
from the extreme censorship of the Media Cleansing Committee.

00:15.910 --> 00:19.290
The conflict between the two continued to escalate.

00:19.970 --> 00:25.730
In the 31st year of Seika, a lone girl plunged herself into the middle of that conflict.

00:33.030 --> 00:37.630
usu murasaki hirogaru

00:33.030 --> 00:37.630
The faint purple spreads across the sky

00:37.630 --> 00:45.610
orenji iro ni kawaru mado no soto

00:37.630 --> 00:45.610
The color changes to orange outside the window

00:45.610 --> 00:49.660
yoru wa mou bai bai

00:45.610 --> 00:49.660
The night's already "bye-bye"

00:50.210 --> 00:55.900
tada kirei na mono wo kirei to

00:50.210 --> 00:55.900
I just want to be someone who

00:55.900 --> 01:00.460
ieru atashi de itai

00:55.900 --> 01:00.460
calls beautiful things beautiful

01:00.460 --> 01:06.800
ima wa dokidoki shitai no

01:00.460 --> 01:06.800
I want to get excited for it!

01:07.330 --> 01:11.860
fumidashichae tomaranai

01:07.330 --> 01:11.860
So I step out, unstoppable

01:11.860 --> 01:16.450
zenbu te ni hairi sou de

01:11.860 --> 01:16.450
And take everything into my own hands

01:16.940 --> 01:21.050
sono saki de aitai

01:16.940 --> 01:21.050
Beyond there, I want to meet

01:21.050 --> 01:27.040
mita koto no nai atashi

01:21.050 --> 01:27.040
the new self that I've never seen

01:27.510 --> 01:32.160
sayonara daisuki na machi

01:27.510 --> 01:32.160
Farewell, my beloved town

01:32.160 --> 01:36.710
atashi mo ganbatte miru yo

01:32.160 --> 01:36.710
I'll try to do my best

01:36.710 --> 01:44.270
kono sora no tsuzuku basho de

01:36.710 --> 01:44.270
somewhere under the same sky

01:48.540 --> 01:50.500
What's going on?!

01:50.500 --> 01:52.780
Tell me the reason!

01:53.120 --> 01:55.890
Escorting key personnel is also one of the Task Force's duties,

01:55.890 --> 01:58.070
so it's nothing special to send some of us to do it.

01:58.510 --> 02:01.270
But why me alone?!

02:02.050 --> 02:04.140
It's to give you more experience.

02:04.290 --> 02:07.250
Then why is Tezuka not included?

02:07.250 --> 02:09.850
Does he not need the experience?!

02:10.140 --> 02:12.230
Don't dupe me!

02:12.660 --> 02:13.830
Fine.

02:14.630 --> 02:17.320
I'll tell you since you seem to be able to handle it.

02:18.430 --> 02:21.840
I judged that you won't be of any use.

02:24.690 --> 02:26.050
Are you satisfied?

02:30.610 --> 02:35.750
Instructor Dojo, you don't trust me?

02:37.820 --> 02:41.240
Why do I do this when I know the result?

02:42.070 --> 02:46.290
Have you done anything that inspires trust?

02:56.690 --> 03:01.140
Situation 04

02:56.690 --> 03:01.140
Recapture the
Library Commander

03:01.460 --> 03:03.790
Frontline ground troops, retreat to the building interior.

03:03.790 --> 03:05.100
Go!

03:12.930 --> 03:15.020
Back us up!

03:35.710 --> 03:39.160
Notice from the Kanto Library Force to the Media Cleansing Force.

03:39.160 --> 03:44.950
The Library Force is abandoning all the remaining publications in the building as of 1140.

03:44.950 --> 03:48.220
All Cleansing Force members have retreated away from the building.

03:48.220 --> 03:49.420
Good work.

04:02.920 --> 04:04.610
All units,

04:04.820 --> 04:08.580
suspicious individuals have entered Mr. Nobeyama's funeral site.

04:09.170 --> 04:11.570
Commander Inamine is under attack.

04:11.570 --> 04:13.780
All units, retreat immediately!

04:13.780 --> 04:15.030
We're returning to base!

04:15.030 --> 04:16.590
Kasahara!

04:19.490 --> 04:25.010
We are the Bakushuukai, an organization that supports the Media Cleansing Committee.

04:25.010 --> 04:30.850
We will be taking custody of the Kanto Library Base Commander, Inamine Kazuichi.

04:31.100 --> 04:32.810
Don't move!

04:34.700 --> 04:37.520
Or we'll blow up the funeral site.

04:41.440 --> 04:47.350
We've arranged for our comrades to take action in case you resist.

04:50.550 --> 04:52.320
I will come with you.

04:53.230 --> 04:54.750
Commander?!

04:57.630 --> 04:59.840
I'll accompany him, too.

05:00.390 --> 05:03.860
I'm Commander Inamine's caretaker.

05:03.860 --> 05:06.930
The well-being of the hostage should be important to you, too.

05:14.050 --> 05:15.930
Fine.

05:21.340 --> 05:23.600
If you follow us, we will blow up the funeral site,

05:23.600 --> 05:26.900
and their lives will not be guaranteed either.

05:38.400 --> 05:43.200
The information they mentioned about the bomb seems to be fake as you thought.

05:43.200 --> 05:45.080
I knew it.

05:45.440 --> 05:49.510
I'm Hiraga from the Metropolitan Police Department's Criminal Affairs Division.

05:50.870 --> 05:53.910
I appreciate your offer to help us today.

05:54.190 --> 05:56.640
We will do our very best.

05:56.990 --> 05:58.450
Genda,

06:00.100 --> 06:01.810
I'm writing everything down.

06:01.810 --> 06:05.190
That's what you intended by bringing me here, right?

06:05.430 --> 06:10.250
I give you permission to disclose this incident in its entirety.

06:10.500 --> 06:13.280
If you're going to write, be sure to write <i>everything</i>.

06:23.170 --> 06:26.130
Hey, don't you have a cushion or something?

06:26.130 --> 06:27.670
Live with it!

06:29.970 --> 06:32.130
I'm sorry, Commander.

06:32.130 --> 06:35.640
It's all right. I'm fine.

06:38.810 --> 06:45.740
Could you report to Instructor Dojo that Kasahara did her job properly when we return to the base?

06:48.520 --> 06:50.570
I promise.

06:52.640 --> 06:56.540
I need to handle this well or I won't feel right about facing him again.

06:56.720 --> 07:00.790
Have you done anything that inspires trust?

07:02.780 --> 07:08.590
Once they contact the base, I'm sure the Library Force will do something about this.

07:10.960 --> 07:15.720
Until then, I will do what I'm supposed to do.

07:35.930 --> 07:37.620
Call trace?

07:39.260 --> 07:40.680
We're good to go.

07:43.410 --> 07:44.400
Hello?

07:44.400 --> 07:49.620
We are the Bakushuukai, the organization that has taken Inamine Kazumichi hostage.

07:49.620 --> 07:54.630
This is LSTC Genda Ryusuke, General Supervisor of the Kanto Library Base Security Team.

07:54.630 --> 07:58.750
I want confirmation of the safety of Commander Inamine and the female librarian taking care of him.

07:59.300 --> 08:01.600
Can you put them on the phone?

08:01.930 --> 08:03.830
Not Inamine.

08:03.470 --> 08:05.540
I'll put the woman on.

08:07.170 --> 08:08.690
Hello.

08:08.690 --> 08:10.570
Kasahara, are you all right?

08:10.570 --> 08:12.810
Yes, somehow.

08:12.810 --> 08:17.530
Oh, could you please tell Shibasaki to cancel our reservation at Tranzar?

08:17.530 --> 08:19.990
We were supposed to mee—

08:19.990 --> 08:22.960
Hey! Can't I at least tell them this?!

08:22.960 --> 08:25.180
It's a really expensive restaurant!

08:25.180 --> 08:28.190
Or are you going to pay for the cancellation fee?!

08:28.460 --> 08:31.930
What kind of nerve does she have?

08:31.930 --> 08:33.390
Hey! Kasahara!

08:33.390 --> 08:34.440
Hello?! Hel—

08:34.440 --> 08:41.610
We are concerned about the library that does not value the privacy and sanctity of public order and tradition.

08:41.610 --> 08:43.470
Therefore, we demand, that in exchange for the lives of the hostages,

08:43.470 --> 08:46.780
all documents taken from the Information Museum be destroyed.

08:46.780 --> 08:49.630
The conditions of the exchange are as follows.

08:49.630 --> 08:54.620
Disclose all the documents you took from the Museum,

08:54.620 --> 08:59.290
match them against the censorship list that the Media Cleansing Committee has publicized,

08:59.290 --> 09:01.220
then burn all the documents.

09:01.220 --> 09:04.030
We will give you two hours to perform those tasks.

09:04.030 --> 09:05.480
We will call you again.

09:09.020 --> 09:11.180
Here's the result from the trace.

09:11.280 --> 09:13.840
The call was made using a mobile phone,

09:13.840 --> 09:17.280
but it was cut off before we could trace the caller's base station.

09:18.650 --> 09:20.970
They jammed the signal...

09:20.970 --> 09:24.250
Hey, someone go get Shibasaki.

09:25.490 --> 09:27.790
She sounded fine.

09:29.450 --> 09:32.210
It was clever...

09:33.080 --> 09:35.130
for that simpleton.

09:35.130 --> 09:36.840
You know about it?

09:36.840 --> 09:40.620
It's a casual restaurant we've been to a few times.

09:40.620 --> 09:43.570
It's not the kind of place you'd need a reservation for,

09:43.570 --> 09:45.590
nor did we plan on going there.

09:45.590 --> 09:47.410
Where is it located?

09:47.410 --> 09:48.810
I believe it's in Tachikawa.

09:48.810 --> 09:51.040
Officers, they're in Tachikawa.

09:51.040 --> 09:53.700
Commander Inamine is in Tachikawa.

09:53.810 --> 09:54.960
All right.

09:54.960 --> 09:59.220
Order our people to narrow down the search to the Tachikawa area, and work on pinpointing the address.

09:59.520 --> 10:01.820
How's the reproduction of the documents coming along?

10:01.820 --> 10:08.670
The Logistical Support Team is working hard, but they're not sure if they'll make it in time.

10:08.850 --> 10:13.950
So we need to work with the possibility of having to comply with their demands.

10:13.950 --> 10:18.510
It won't be too bad if they really cease their actions after we comply.

10:22.250 --> 10:24.640
I'll go check on the Logistical Support Team.

10:26.300 --> 10:28.030
I can do that.

10:28.160 --> 10:30.290
Let him do it.

10:44.770 --> 10:46.850
It doesn't make any sense!

10:47.740 --> 10:51.340
I judged that you won't be of any use.

11:00.360 --> 11:01.780
Damn it!

11:02.880 --> 11:06.380
I wonder if they figured out that message?

11:08.310 --> 11:10.680
I'm sure they have.

11:10.680 --> 11:13.210
If they just ask Shibasaki...

11:14.860 --> 11:16.340
What are you trying to do?!

11:17.290 --> 11:19.790
I would like to take off my artificial leg.

11:19.790 --> 11:22.070
The attachment must have shifted, giving me quite a sore.

11:25.700 --> 11:27.500
Let the woman do it.

11:27.610 --> 11:29.840
Would you please?

11:29.840 --> 11:33.000
I've never done this, so please walk me through it.

11:35.140 --> 11:39.420
This is the leg that fought in the Hino Nightmare.

11:40.620 --> 11:45.530
We're standing on the path that was paved by this leg.

11:57.790 --> 12:00.150
Commander Inamine's leg came off!

12:00.150 --> 12:01.820
What?!

12:02.140 --> 12:04.170
I have the coordinates!

12:04.370 --> 12:07.740
Match it up against the newest residential map!

12:08.080 --> 12:09.170
What?

12:09.170 --> 12:10.560
What's going on?

12:10.560 --> 12:17.020
There's a mechanism in the Commander's leg that triggers a transmitter if it's detached in a certain way.

12:17.020 --> 12:18.660
A transmitter?!

12:18.660 --> 12:20.060
I got it!

12:20.060 --> 12:24.160
It's coming from a new, unpopulated town, in a newly-constructed building.

12:24.160 --> 12:27.890
All right. Task Force, prepare to move out!

12:28.040 --> 12:30.640
We'll seize them before they call us again.

12:30.640 --> 12:32.350
Wait!

12:32.520 --> 12:36.160
Now that we know the location, we'll take command.

12:36.160 --> 12:40.160
Let us handle the rest our way.

12:40.160 --> 12:42.850
I can't let you do as you wish!

12:42.850 --> 12:44.570
Let the police handle it!

12:44.570 --> 12:52.990
Sorry, but past experience doesn't say much about your ability to follow through with the operation.

12:52.990 --> 12:54.430
Am I wrong?

12:55.390 --> 13:03.470
But, without a formal request, the Library Force's right to fire is limited to within library facilities.

13:04.540 --> 13:07.600
I told you we'll do it our way.

13:07.930 --> 13:12.730
We'll deploy our troops as if the buildings at the location are a future library site!

13:12.730 --> 13:15.140
Agree to whatever price they quote!

13:15.140 --> 13:18.480
Quiet the audit with whatever it takes!

13:19.480 --> 13:21.400
This is absurd!

13:21.400 --> 13:23.360
This is how we handle things.

13:23.360 --> 13:27.440
But do you realize how many hundreds of millions of yen this will cost?!

13:27.440 --> 13:34.390
This new town is pretty big, so there's a high possibility that a library will be opened there.

13:34.390 --> 13:37.310
Well, you could call it an anticipatory investment.

13:37.310 --> 13:40.520
In the worst case scenario, paying a cancellation penalty will take care of it.

13:41.980 --> 13:43.650
Dojo!

13:44.860 --> 13:46.370
I'll leave it to you.

13:46.370 --> 13:47.720
Do as you want.

13:49.320 --> 13:50.720
Yes, Sir!

13:55.350 --> 13:59.230
Why do you resemble me so much?

14:00.530 --> 14:04.190
My old... idiotic self...

14:08.290 --> 14:10.230
Being careless without thinking of the consequences,

14:10.230 --> 14:12.790
emotionally fragile,

14:12.790 --> 14:14.330
all those...

14:17.580 --> 14:19.290
things I left behind.

14:19.290 --> 14:22.830
Why do you bring them back to me with such a passion?!

14:26.830 --> 14:32.390
I couldn't help but distance you from me every time you pushed yourself too hard.

14:34.220 --> 14:38.110
I hurt you just so I could protect my fragile self.

14:39.640 --> 14:41.200
It was all my fault.

14:41.200 --> 14:42.830
I realize it now.

14:42.830 --> 14:47.670
So, for God's sake, be safe!

15:04.550 --> 15:07.310
Is it still sore?

15:07.310 --> 15:09.100
Do you want me to rub it?

15:09.100 --> 15:13.030
Now that I took my leg off, I'm fine.

15:41.750 --> 15:46.360
Maybe they hit a wall in the investigation with such a vague hint.

15:49.640 --> 15:51.920
Please hear this, Kasahara!

16:10.950 --> 16:13.050
Instructor Dojo?!

16:15.260 --> 16:17.430
I'll have to be rough on you.

16:17.730 --> 16:19.260
One...

16:19.880 --> 16:21.430
Two...

16:22.160 --> 16:23.680
Three!

16:34.550 --> 16:36.300
Damn it!

16:38.300 --> 16:39.920
Stay down!

16:43.350 --> 16:44.750
Are you all right?!

16:47.240 --> 16:49.950
Yes, Sir!

16:58.230 --> 17:01.630
Thank you for what you did today.

17:01.630 --> 17:06.100
I will make sure to tell Dojo about your performance.

17:06.810 --> 17:08.810
Thank you, Sir.

17:14.610 --> 17:15.980
Instructor Dojo...

17:15.980 --> 17:17.830
You did well.

17:18.860 --> 17:22.530
I take back what I said about you being of no use.

17:22.530 --> 17:23.890
Forgive me.

17:26.240 --> 17:28.540
How vexing!

17:30.140 --> 17:37.050
It's not something you need my forgiveness for.

17:38.080 --> 17:39.420
Is that so?

17:39.420 --> 17:40.660
Fine, then.

17:41.050 --> 17:43.530
If I...

17:45.650 --> 17:49.350
Oh, it's nothing after all.

17:50.050 --> 17:53.090
It wouldn't be a problem if you resigned.

17:53.970 --> 17:57.350
But we'd probably miss you.

17:58.060 --> 17:59.790
Damn it!

17:59.790 --> 18:04.580
I didn't expect for it to feel this good to be recognized by him!

18:07.180 --> 18:08.680
I won't quit!

18:08.680 --> 18:13.380
I'm going to surpass you, so I'll never quit!

18:14.280 --> 18:17.720
Do you intend not to quit even when you reach the retirement age?

18:18.580 --> 18:20.620
What do you mean?!

18:20.620 --> 18:23.530
That's very rude!

18:23.530 --> 18:24.590
You're the rude one!

18:24.590 --> 18:25.890
Know your place!

18:26.590 --> 18:28.000
Shut up!

18:28.000 --> 18:29.460
I swear I'll surpass you!

18:29.460 --> 18:31.520
Not in your lifetime!

18:30.110 --> 18:32.210
There she goes again.

18:31.520 --> 18:33.160
How do you know?!

18:32.210 --> 18:35.830
They really are alike.

18:33.160 --> 18:34.930
We'll never know unless we try!

18:34.930 --> 18:36.670
Are you an idiot?!

18:35.830 --> 18:38.640
That's enough.

18:48.150 --> 18:51.080
I can't date you after all.

18:53.290 --> 18:59.770
Actually, that you're not feeling anything is a sign that you don't love me.

19:00.000 --> 19:03.360
I don't love you either.

19:04.160 --> 19:06.970
That's so blatant.

19:06.970 --> 19:11.770
Anyway, where did you even get the idea of dating me?

19:12.810 --> 19:20.490
LOSC Dojo mentioned something about things I could learn from you, so I became curious.

19:21.690 --> 19:23.470
Huh?!

19:23.470 --> 19:24.960
Are you serious?

19:24.960 --> 19:26.190
That's dumb.

19:26.190 --> 19:29.950
So, you love your superior, not me!

19:29.950 --> 19:34.420
Besides, wanting to date me because of that is so detached!

19:34.420 --> 19:38.570
I feel like an idiot getting so serious over it!

19:39.490 --> 19:40.800
This is pissing me off!

19:40.800 --> 19:43.780
It was a waste of time mulling over it!

19:47.610 --> 19:51.850
You're really funny as a friend.

19:58.020 --> 20:00.140
Shut up already!

20:00.140 --> 20:02.720
Stop laughing at me!

20:06.980 --> 20:09.170
I'm back.

20:09.950 --> 20:12.500
I bought some cake.

20:13.000 --> 20:15.140
What are you doing?

20:15.140 --> 20:19.920
I'm thinking about writing home.

20:21.040 --> 20:23.250
You're finally doing it.

20:23.250 --> 20:24.590
Yeah.

20:24.590 --> 20:28.580
But I'm stuck about what to write.

20:28.580 --> 20:30.610
Too bad,

20:31.000 --> 20:34.560
you're a bit too late.

20:41.890 --> 20:45.890
I hope you are doing well. It has already been half a year since you started working in the library. I'm sure you are getting used to the work by now. I heard that the department you work for does not get exposed to danger. But knowing how libraries are constantly involved in ominous incidents, we never know if you might get involved in one. We are both very concerned about your safety. However, we are still glad and proud to see you stepping into society, and starting work as an adult.

20:45.890 --> 20:50.990
We are thinking about coming to see your workplace and how you do your job. I look forward to seeing you!
- Mom, Dad.

21:00.260 --> 21:02.300
No way!

21:02.300 --> 21:04.390
No way! No way! No way! No way!

21:04.390 --> 21:06.180
What do I do now?!

21:06.690 --> 21:10.030
nani ka ga kawaru kigashita

21:06.690 --> 21:10.030
I had a feeling something was about to change

21:10.030 --> 21:13.410
nani mo kawaranu asa ni

21:10.030 --> 21:13.410
on this very ordinary morning

21:13.410 --> 21:18.420
itsu mo yori sukoshi ii mezamedatta

21:13.410 --> 21:18.420
I woke up feeling a little better than usual

21:20.080 --> 21:26.760
hito sashiyubi de sashimesu no wa mirai

21:20.080 --> 21:26.760
My index finger points out to the future

21:26.760 --> 21:36.430
kimi no te no hira ga fureru tabi ni afuru omoi

21:26.760 --> 21:36.430
My thoughts overflow each time I touch your palm

21:36.880 --> 21:40.410
ch-ch-ch-changes saa kawatteku

21:36.880 --> 21:40.410
Changes, yeah. I'm changing.

21:40.410 --> 21:43.730
sayonara furui jibun

21:40.410 --> 21:43.730
Goodbye my old self

21:43.730 --> 21:50.260
shingenjitsu atarashii nani ka ga matteru

21:43.730 --> 21:50.260
There's something new awaiting me in the new reality

21:50.260 --> 21:54.000
ch-ch-ch-changes saa kawatteku

21:50.260 --> 21:54.000
Changes, yeah. I'm changing.

21:54.000 --> 21:57.230
ushinau mono mo aru

21:54.000 --> 21:57.230
There are things I'll lose too

21:57.230 --> 22:03.000
demo iindesu hitotsu unazuki kakedasu

21:57.230 --> 22:03.000
But that's okay, I'll just nod and keep running

22:03.000 --> 22:10.550
saa subete ga ima kawatteku subete ga hajimaru

22:03.000 --> 22:10.550
Yeah, everything is changing now, everything starts now

22:10.550 --> 22:20.840
shingenjitsu dare no mono demo nai atarashii jibun

22:10.550 --> 22:20.840
It's a new reality, my new self belongs to no one but me
